@startuml Component State Machine

[*] -d-> Terminated
Terminated -> Starting : Component is started in its configured sandbox.\nAll dependencies are ready and the component is\nconfigured to run in the currently active Run Target.
Starting --> Ready : The component\nReady Condition is fulfilled.
Ready --> Terminating : Component is being terminated (e.g. due to Run Target change)
Terminating --> Terminated : Component is now terminated\n(this may have required <color:red>forceful termination</color>\n<color:red>if component violated the shutdown timeout</color>).

state Fault #red
Ready -[#red]-> Fault : <color:red>Supervision failure</color>.
Starting -[#red]-> Fault : <color:red>Component crashed</color>\nor <color:red>Ready Condition timeout</color>.
Ready -[#red]-> Fault : <color:red>Component crashed</color>

Fault -[#red]-> Terminating : <color:red>Recovery action (Restart, Run Target change, etc.)</color>.

legend right
	Error cases are highlighted in <color:red>red</color>.
endlegend

@enduml
